# Our Little World Project Notes

- This is the modernized Our Little World Expo/React Native app in the GitHub repo `jakrim/ourLittleWorld`.
- Work from `master` unless the user asks for a separate branch. `old_jessLaurApp` preserves the pre-Our Little World master state.
- The app uses Expo Router under `app/`; shared screens, providers, Supabase/data access, photo scanning, and UI primitives live under `src/`.
- Old JessLaurApp birthday/archive code belongs only on `old_jessLaurApp`; do not reintroduce archive routes, static memory data, or generated simulator app bundles on `master`.
- Do not commit generated build outputs. Keep `build/`, `dist/`, `ios/build/`, `android/build/`, `.expo/`, simulator screenshots, and seed-photo scratch files out of Git.
- Treat `.env`, `.env.local`, Apple signing files, and EAS credentials as local secrets. Update `.env.example` only with placeholder keys.
- Before pushing, check `git status --short --branch` and make sure large simulator/native build products are not staged.
- Documents created for Jesse to review should be HTML by default, including audits, plans, reviews, summaries, specs, and comparisons. Use Markdown only for repo-native docs or when Jesse explicitly asks for Markdown.
- Expo MCP is a first-class debugging/build aid. Keep normal Metro startup MCP-free, but actively use remote Expo MCP for docs, SDK, dependency, config/plugin, and EAS/build questions. Use local Expo MCP via `pnpm dev:mobile:mcp` or `pnpm --filter @ourlittleworld/mobile start:mcp` for screenshots, taps, `testID` lookup, logs, React Native DevTools, Expo Router sitemap, route debugging, native UI verification, and post-fix visual checks. Reconnect or restart the MCP connection after starting or stopping the local MCP-enabled dev server.
